{:edb/db-before-t 1139 :edb/db-after-t 1140 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534452 50 #inst "2026-10-11T20:58:25.902Z" 13194139534452 17592186045417 true] [17592186122192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122193 13194139534452 17592186045417 false] [17592186122192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122194 13194139534452 17592186045417 false] [17592186122192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122195 13194139534452 17592186045417 false] [17592186122192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122196 13194139534452 17592186045417 false] [17592186122192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186122197 13194139534452 17592186045417 false] [17592186122192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421993 13194139534452 17592186045417 true] [17592186122192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186421997 13194139534452 17592186045417 true] [17592186122192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186422000 13194139534452 17592186045417 true] [17592186122192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186422001 13194139534452 17592186045417 true] [17592186122192 1075 #edb/ref 17592186422002 13194139534452 17592186045417 true] [17592186122192 1078 #edb/ref 17592186421997 13194139534452 17592186045417 true] [17592186122234 1078 #edb/ref 17592186122236 13194139534452 17592186045417 true] [17592186124442 1038 #edb/ref 17592186422010 13194139534452 17592186045417 true] [17592186124442 1038 #edb/ref 17592186422011 13194139534452 17592186045417 true] [17592186124932 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534452 17592186045417 true] [17592186124932 1071 "Find $f_{xy}(x, y) + f_{yx}(x, y)$ given that $f_{x}(x, y) = 2x\\sin y$ and $f_{y}(x, y) = x^{2}\\cos y$." 13194139534452 17592186045417 false] [17592186124932 1071 "Find ${f}_{xy}(x,y)+{f}_{yx}(x,y)$ given that  ${f}_{x}(x,y)=2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.$" 13194139534452 17592186045417 true] [17592186124932 1074 "To find ${f}_{xy}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find ${f}_{yx}(x,y)$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{y}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y)+{f}_{yx}(x,y) & =2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\  & =4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534452 17592186045417 true] [17592186124939 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534452 17592186045417 true] [17592186124939 1071 "Calculate $f_{xyx}(x, y)$ given that $f(x, y) = x^{2}y + y^{2}\\ln y$." 13194139534452 17592186045417 false] [17592186124939 1071 "Calculate ${f}_{xyx}(x,y)$ given that $f(x,y)={x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y.$" 13194139534452 17592186045417 true] [17592186124939 1074 "First, we find the first-order derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) \\\\  & =2xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${f}_{xy}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({f}_{x}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2xy) \\\\  & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find ${f}_{xyx}(x,y)$ by differentiating ${f}_{xy}(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xyx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({f}_{xy}(x,y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534452 17592186045417 true] [17592186421992 1043 #edb/ref 17592186422012 13194139534452 17592186045417 true] [17592186421992 1043 #edb/ref 17592186422013 13194139534452 17592186045417 true] [17592186421992 1043 #edb/ref 17592186422014 13194139534452 17592186045417 true] [17592186421992 1043 #edb/ref 17592186422015 13194139534452 17592186045417 true] [17592186421992 1043 #edb/ref 17592186422016 13194139534452 17592186045417 true] [17592186421992 1044 #edb/r